"""Lesson-specific student content. Executed by build-pages.py."""
import re

app_name='Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson01-app'
port=3100
learning=[
 ('Install the SDK','Create a Node project, choose TypeScript, install the Agent SDK and run TypeScript with tsx.'),
 ('Set the key in the same shell','Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in PowerShell or Bash before starting the agent. Child processes inherit it; another terminal does not inherit a later assignment.'),
 ('Ask the first question','Submit exactly “What files are here?” and print the assistant text and final outcome.'),
 ('Choose a working directory','cwd points to sample-workspace. The question refers to that directory, not your entire computer or the folder holding .env.'),
 ('Observe a real tool call','Glob lists file paths. tools makes it available; allowedTools pre-approves it. Shell, file-reading and editing tools are not enabled.'),
 ('Check completion','A tool request and assistant text are progress. Check the final result subtype and error flag before reporting success.')]

setup='''mkdir my-agent
cd my-agent
npm init -y
npm pkg set type=module
npm install @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk@0.3.310
npm install --save-dev tsx typescript @types/node
mkdir sample-workspace
"Hello, students!" | Set-Content sample-workspace/notes.txt'''
shell='$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = "your_api_key"\n# Check presence without printing the key:\nnode -e "console.log(Boolean(process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY))"'
bash='export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="your_api_key"\nnode -e \'console.log(Boolean(process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY))\''
clone=f'git clone https://github.com/luiscoco/{app_name}.git\ncd .\\{app_name}\nnpm ci'
local='cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson01-getting-started\nnpm ci'
agent=(APP/'src/agent.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
sample=(APP/'src/sample.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
standalone=(APP/'examples/first-agent.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
server=(APP/'src/server.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
client=(APP/'src/client.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
def excerpt(source,start,end):return source[source.index(start):source.index(end,source.index(start))].strip()
walk=[
 ('01','Install a TypeScript project','package.json','The SDK is the runtime dependency. tsx executes TypeScript; type=module enables ES modules. npm ci reproduces this completed app from its lockfile.',setup,'powershell'),
 ('02','Pass the key through the process environment','src/sample.ts','The terminal sample does not load .env. It checks the inherited environment before creating a query. npm run sample:env explicitly loads the optional local file instead.',excerpt(sample,'if (!process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY','const conversation'),'typescript'),
 ('03','Give the agent a small directory and Glob','src/agent.ts','The fixed cwd is sample-workspace. Only Glob is available and pre-approved. Four SDK turns leave room for discovery and a final answer; one query call can contain several model turns.',excerpt(agent,'export function lessonOptions','export type LabEvent'),'typescript'),
 ('04','Ask the exact first question','src/sample.ts','query receives the literal lesson prompt through DEFAULT_PROMPT and returns an async iterator. The same options power the CLI and the web lab.',excerpt(sample,'const conversation','try {'),'typescript'),
 ('05','Print tool activity, text and the final result','src/sample.ts','Print only human-readable text and tool names, followed by the final subtype. is_error also matters even when a subtype says success. finally closes the query object.',excerpt(sample,'try {','\n} finally')+'\n} finally {\n  conversation.close();\n}','typescript'),
 ('06','Forward selected events to the browser','src/agent.ts','The host projects text, tool calls and the final result into student-facing events. It does not send the API key or raw runtime configuration.',excerpt(agent,'export function projectMessage','export async function runAgent'),'typescript'),
 ('07','Compare answer with real local evidence','src/client.ts','The host reads the demo directory for a labelled reference list. That reference is not supplied to query as an answer. The browser uses textContent, and the live recording verifies an actual Glob call.',excerpt(client,'async function configure','$("form")'),'typescript')]

document('/','What files <em>are here?</em>','Install the SDK. Set your API key in the same shell. Run your first agent and print the results.',
 '<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Install</b><p>Choose TypeScript</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Configure</b><p>Set the key in this shell</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Run</b><p>Ask which files are here</p></div></div><section class="workspace"><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR FIRST FILE-DISCOVERY AGENT</p><h2>Ask the sample question</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta" role="status">Checking configuration…</p><form id="form"><label for="prompt">Prompt</label><textarea id="prompt" maxlength="2000" required></textarea><p class="meta">Model: <strong id="model">—</strong><br>Tool: Glob · Working directory: sample-workspace<br>Up to 4 turns · SDK budget: $0.15</p><button class="primary" id="run" disabled>Run query() →</button></form><h3 style="margin-top:28px">Expected files · host reference</h3><pre id="files"></pre><p class="meta">This reference comes from the local host. Claude must discover the files using Glob.</p></article><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">REAL SDK OUTPUT</p><h2>Read the results</h2><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><span>Status</span><strong id="status" role="status">Ready</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>Turns</span><strong id="turns">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>Estimated cost</span><strong id="cost">—</strong></div></div><div id="answer" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="meta">SDK session ID: <span id="session">—</span></p><details open><summary>Observe the SDK messages and tool call</summary><ol id="events"></ol></details></article></section><aside class="note">The question refers to <strong>sample-workspace</strong>, a small demo folder with three committed files. Only the listing tool Glob is enabled; Bash, Read and editing tools are not enabled. This local teaching example is not an operating-system sandbox. Wait for the final result before navigating away; closing the page cancels this app’s run.</aside>'+actions(('/learn.html','What you will learn →'),('/run.html','Configure and run →')), '<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')

document('/learn.html','Your first <em>three steps.</em>','Understand installation, shell configuration and a real file-discovery run before adding more capabilities.',cards(learning)+'<section class="step"><h2>Choose your language</h2><p>This complete application uses <strong>TypeScript</strong>, following the course preference. Python is also supported by the Agent SDK; its package name is <code>claude-agent-sdk</code>, installed with <code>pip install claude-agent-sdk</code>. The commands, source files and tests in this app use Node, npm and TypeScript.</p><p>Use the <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/quickstart">official quickstart</a> for the Python alternative. Do not mix a Python virtual environment’s commands with the TypeScript run instructions.</p></section><section class="note"><strong>Try explaining:</strong> What does “here” mean? Why does setting a key in a different terminal not configure this process? Why are tools and allowedTools separate options? Why can one query need more than one model turn?</section>'+actions(('/','← Application lab'),('/run.html','Installation and run steps →')))

run='<section class="step"><span class="number">01</span><h2>Install the SDK and choose TypeScript</h2><p>For this app use Node.js 24 or newer, npm, and a model-accessible Anthropic API key. On Windows, Git for Windows may be needed for Git Bash. Start a new project using:</p>'+snippet(setup,'powershell')+'<p>This teaches installation from scratch. Save the standalone source shown below as <code>agent.ts</code> in that project. For the completed application, clone it instead:</p>'+snippet(clone,'powershell')+'<p>In the original presentations workspace, the local directory is:</p>'+snippet(local,'powershell')+'</section>'
run+='<section class="step"><span class="number">02</span><h2>Set your API key in the same shell</h2><p>In the PowerShell terminal that will run the agent, replace the placeholder with your own key. The presence check prints only true or false.</p>'+snippet(shell,'powershell')+'<p>macOS/Linux Bash alternative:</p>'+snippet(bash,'bash')+'<p>This assignment applies to the current shell and its child processes. Repeat it in a new terminal. The SDK does not automatically read .env. Keep the key out of code and Git.</p></section>'
run+='<section class="step"><span class="number">03</span><h2>Run the sample and print results</h2><p>From the completed application root, in the same configured shell:</p>'+snippet('npm run sample','powershell')+'<p>The sample asks exactly <strong>What files are here?</strong>. Watch for a Glob tool call, the names <code>notes.txt</code>, <code>src/hello.ts</code> and <code>todo.md</code>, and a final success result. Wording, turn count and cost can vary. A tool round trip often needs more than one model turn.</p><p>For your from-scratch project, run <code>npx tsx agent.ts</code> instead. Its folder contains the demo file you created in step 1.</p></section>'
run+='<section class="step"><span class="number">04</span><h2>Optional: use a local .env file explicitly</h2><p>For repeated classroom runs, copy the safe template without overwriting an existing file:</p>'+snippet('if (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm run sample:env','powershell')+snippet('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3100','dotenv')+'<p>The <code>sample:env</code> script explicitly loads this file through Node’s startup option. A key already set in the shell takes precedence. To use only the file in this PowerShell session, first run <code>Remove-Item Env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue</code>. On Windows, if needed, add <code>CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe</code>.</p></section>'
run+='<section class="step"><span class="number">05</span><h2>Run the web application</h2>'+snippet('npm start\n# Open http://127.0.0.1:3100','powershell')+'<p>The web command loads an optional .env file too. Keep its terminal open. Click Run query once, compare the response with the host reference, then follow the architecture and code pages. Starting the server makes no model request. Each submitted prompt may incur API usage. Stop the server with Ctrl+C when finished.</p></section>'
run+='<section class="step"><span class="number">06</span><h2>Inspect the standalone sample and check your work</h2>'+snippet(standalone)+'<p>For the completed app:</p>'+snippet('npm test\n# After editing src/client.ts:\nnpm run build:client\n# Refresh student pages from source:\npython scripts/build-pages.py','powershell')+'<p>Exercise: add a harmless file inside sample-workspace, refresh the browser reference and run the same question again. Explain why the result changes without changing the prompt.</p></section>'
run+='<section class="step"><h2>Troubleshooting</h2><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>What to check</th></tr><tr><td>Missing key</td><td>Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in this terminal before npm run sample, or explicitly use sample:env.</td></tr><tr><td>Authentication/model error</td><td>Check the active shell key, model access and billing. Restart the web server after configuration changes.</td></tr><tr><td>Runtime/Git Bash missing</td><td>Run npm ci with optional dependencies enabled. Check the Git Bash executable path on Windows.</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong files</td><td>Check cwd. This app deliberately points to sample-workspace, not the repository root.</td></tr><tr><td>Limit result</td><td>Read the actual final subtype. Tool activity alone is not success.</td></tr><tr><td>Port in use</td><td>If this app is already running, open its printed URL. Stop its original terminal with Ctrl+C to restart. For another service, choose a different PORT.</td></tr></table></div></section>'
document('/run.html','Install. Configure. <em>Run.</em>','Follow the three beginner steps, then try the same agent in the browser.',run+actions(('/learn.html','← Learning goals'),('/','Run the web sample →')))

lanes=['Student','Browser + host','Agent SDK','Claude API','Demo folder']
arrows=[(0,1,'1. Ask: What files are here?'),(1,1,'2. Check inherited key and input'),(1,2,'3. query(prompt, options); cwd set'),(2,3,'4. Send prompt and Glob tool definition'),(3,2,'5. Request Glob file discovery'),(2,4,'6. Run Glob in sample-workspace'),(4,2,'7. Return matching file paths'),(2,3,'8. Send the tool result to Claude'),(3,2,'9. Produce the final answer'),(2,1,'10. Yield tool, text and result messages'),(1,1,'11. Print results or render safe text'),(1,0,'12. Compare files; check final status')]
xs=[160,490,820,1150,1480];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1640" height="1530" viewBox="0 0 1640 1530"><title>Install, configure, run: Agent SDK file discovery</title><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1640" height="1530" fill="white"/><text x="40" y="52" font-size="32" font-family="Arial" font-weight="bold" fill="#101a44">What files are here? · one query with a real Glob call</text>']
for i,(x,label) in enumerate(zip(xs,lanes)):
 colour=['#087fff','#8838ff','#8838ff','#00a977','#087fff'][i]
 svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-145}" y="90" width="290" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" font-weight="bold" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1480" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 a,b=xs[a],xs[b];y=250+i*105
 path=f'M{a} {y} h55 v22 h-55' if a==b else f'M{a} {y} H{b}'
 svg.append(f'<text x="{min(a,b)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="26">{escape(label)}</text><path d="{path}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
svg.append('</svg>');(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg),encoding='utf-8')
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps({'lanes':lanes,'arrows':arrows},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
body='<section class="step"><h2>Before the first message</h2><p>Install the dependencies, set the key in the launching shell, and choose the working directory. The SDK starts a local runtime; Claude inference happens through the configured provider. No Managed Agents agent or environment IDs are required.</p><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download the UML SVG</a></section><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Twelve-step UML sequence from the student question through a Glob call to the final result"></div>'
explanations=[
 'The browser submits the exact question. The terminal sample supplies the same constant without needing a web server.',
 'The launching process must inherit a key. The browser host also validates the prompt before starting the runtime.',
 'The host creates one query object. Its options select sample-workspace as cwd and make only Glob available.',
 'The runtime sends the task and the Glob tool definition to the model. It does not supply the browser reference list as an answer.',
 'The model chooses Glob. An assistant tool_use block exposes the requested tool and pattern as observable progress.',
 'The SDK executes the built-in listing tool locally. This does not require a Bash command or a Read tool.',
 'The local tool returns the file paths it actually found, including the nested src/hello.ts file.',
 'The SDK handles the next model interaction with the tool result. The host does not implement a manual Messages API loop.',
 'Claude produces a human-readable answer informed by the returned paths. The wording may vary across runs.',
 'The same async iterator yields progress and a final SDK result. One query call can include multiple model turns.',
 'The terminal prints selected output with console.log; the browser renders projected events using textContent.',
 'Compare the named files with the demo folder and inspect the final result status. Text or a tool call alone does not establish completion.']
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows,1):
 body+=f'<section class="step"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h3>{escape(label)}</h3><p>{escape(lanes[a])} → {escape(lanes[b])}. '+explanations[i-1]+'</p></section>'
body+='<section class="note">One query call can contain a model → tool → model round trip. The browser does not provide a prewritten answer. Its host reference list is separate from the agent’s discovery. Only Glob is available, and cwd is a working-directory choice rather than an operating-system sandbox.</section>'+actions(('/','← Application lab'),('/walkthrough.html','Follow the source →'))
document('/architecture.html','Trace the <em>workflow.</em>','A UML sequence connects the first question, local file discovery and the final result.',body)
body='<section class="step"><h2>Small standalone sample</h2><p>Run from the project root after setting the key in this shell. The full web app adds input checks and browser transport.</p>'+snippet(standalone)+'</section>'
for n,title,source,explanation,code,language in walk:
 body+=f'<section class="step"><span class="number">{n}</span><h2>{escape(title)}</h2><p>{escape(explanation)}</p><p class="source">Source: {escape(source)}</p>'+snippet(code,language)+'</section>'
document('/walkthrough.html','Explain each <em>code step.</em>','Read the actual installation, environment, query and result-handling code.',body+actions(('/architecture.html','← UML sequence'),('/','Try the sample →')))

readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 01 · Install, configure and run\n\nTeach the first three steps: install the SDK, set an API key in the same shell, and ask **What files are here?** This complete TypeScript app includes five linked student pages, a UML SVG, coloured code snippets and the course visual assets.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+'\n'.join('- '+title+': '+description for title,description in learning)
readme+='\n\n## Configure and run the completed application\n\n```powershell\n'+clone+'\n'+shell+'\nnpm run sample\n```\n\nUse your own key; the example is a placeholder. Keep the same terminal. The terminal sample does not load .env automatically. For the original presentations workspace, use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson01-getting-started` instead of the clone commands.\n\nOptional .env workflow:\n\n```powershell\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm run sample:env\nnpm start\n```\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:3100. Keep the terminal open; Ctrl+C stops it. The web start command explicitly loads an optional .env file. A shell key takes precedence over the file. Restart after edits. Use the printed URL if PORT changes. Starting the server does not call Claude.\n\n```dotenv\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3100\n```\n\nOn Windows, if needed, add `CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe`. Use Node.js 24+, keep optional npm dependencies enabled, and select a model your account can access.\n\n## Create a new TypeScript project from scratch\n\n```powershell\n'+setup+'\n```\n\nCopy examples/first-agent.ts into that project as agent.ts. Set the key in that shell, then run `npx tsx agent.ts`. TypeScript is the implemented language for this lab; the official SDK also supports Python.\n\n## Expected evidence\n\nThe completed app points cwd at sample-workspace. Expect a real Glob tool call and these relative paths: notes.txt, src/hello.ts, todo.md. The assistant wording, number of model turns and estimated cost can vary. A final success subtype with is_error false establishes completion. The labelled browser reference list comes from the host and is not passed to query as its answer.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for n,title,source,explanation,code,language in walk:readme+=f'### {n}. {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\nSource: [{source}]({source})\n\n```{language}\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Student pages and maintenance\n\nThe application navigation links the lab, learning goals, setup/run guide, UML architecture and code walkthrough. All pages use large text, the shared light/dark preference, syntax colouring and bundled visual assets.\n\n```powershell\nnpm test\nnpm run build:client\npython scripts/build-pages.py\n```\n\nThe generator works with bundled assets and needs no sibling lesson. Tests check prompt/message handling, demo-directory options and duplicate-start behaviour without API calls. If this app is already listening, a second npm start prints its URL. If another service owns the port, stop it or choose a different PORT.\n\n## Scope and repository contents\n\nGlob is the only available tool. The sample enables no shell, file-reading or editing tool, no MCP servers or plugins, and no transcript persistence. A fixed cwd and instructions are not an operating-system sandbox. This is a trusted local teaching app, not a multi-user service. Four turns and a small SDK budget bound the exercise but do not guarantee billing. Closing the web connection cancels this app’s local run.\n\nSource, student pages, demo files, tests, lockfile and visual assets are included. Videos, audio, PowerPoint files, teaching-material, dependencies and the real .env remain local and are ignored by Git.\n\n## Official references\n\n- [Agent SDK quickstart: installation and environment authentication](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/quickstart)\n- [Tool availability and permissions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions)\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
(APP/'scripts/walkthrough-data.json').write_text(json.dumps([dict(number=n,title=t,source=s,explanation=e,code=c,language=l) for n,t,s,e,c,l in walk],indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
(APP/'scripts/source-hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps({p:hashlib.sha256((APP/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in ['src/agent.ts','src/sample.ts','src/server.ts','src/client.ts','package.json']},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five lesson-specific pages, UML, source snippets and README.')
